WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.080 --> 00:00:01.930
So let's talk about voting by mail.

00:00:01.930 --> 00:00:06.240
Very important issue in general, very important
issue acutely so right now, because if the

00:00:06.240 --> 00:00:13.910
Corona virus pandemic I have for you today,
Exhibit A about why Donald Trump is scared

00:00:13.910 --> 00:00:19.310
to death and completely opposed to the November
presidential election being done as a vote

00:00:19.310 --> 00:00:20.850
by mail election.

00:00:20.850 --> 00:00:22.220
And the reason is very simple.

00:00:22.220 --> 00:00:24.560
Vote by mail means more people vote.

00:00:24.560 --> 00:00:26.859
More people voting is not good for Donald
Trump.

00:00:26.859 --> 00:00:29.289
And it is generally not good for the Republican
Party.

00:00:29.289 --> 00:00:31.440
The example comes from Kansas.

00:00:31.440 --> 00:00:37.400
Kansas Democrats decided to do this year's
primary or caucus as vote by mail.

00:00:37.400 --> 00:00:40.690
This is the Democratic selection in 2016.

00:00:40.690 --> 00:00:47.240
Kansas voted in person and about thirty nine
thousand people voted thirty nine thousand

00:00:47.240 --> 00:00:51.220
in 2020 because of the pandemic, its vote
by mail.

00:00:51.220 --> 00:00:57.660
And they have already had one hundred and
thirty eight thousand people votes.

00:00:57.660 --> 00:01:01.160
And this is considering that the outcome is
a foregone conclusion.

00:01:01.160 --> 00:01:04.570
Joe Biden is the only candidate left.

00:01:04.570 --> 00:01:05.570
Everybody else has dropped out.

00:01:05.570 --> 00:01:06.730
Bernie's gone.

00:01:06.730 --> 00:01:11.510
And still with vote by mail this year, we
have a turnout in Kansas.

00:01:11.510 --> 00:01:15.800
That is three and a half times that of 2016.

00:01:15.800 --> 00:01:19.560
There is almost nothing to vote for in a sense.

00:01:19.560 --> 00:01:25.180
And turnout is orders of magnitude greater
than what it was in 2016.

00:01:25.180 --> 00:01:31.630
So we know that vote by mail in November of
2020 would be a turnout boosting mechanism.

00:01:31.630 --> 00:01:33.330
We know that even pandemic aside.

00:01:33.330 --> 00:01:38.600
I mean, just in a normal election, letting
everybody vote, vote by mail would likely

00:01:38.600 --> 00:01:40.490
increase turnout.

00:01:40.490 --> 00:01:44.020
And that's not good for Republicans and that's
not good for Trump.

00:01:44.020 --> 00:01:48.620
Why do you think they've spent 20 years trying
to reduce the number of people that are voting?

00:01:48.620 --> 00:01:53.350
Now, there are some other factors here which
could account for this huge rise in the number

00:01:53.350 --> 00:01:57.430
of people voting in the Democratic caucus
in Kansas.

00:01:57.430 --> 00:02:03.820
One is, you know, maybe there's a motivation
to vote against Donald Trump in November for

00:02:03.820 --> 00:02:04.820
Democrats.

00:02:04.820 --> 00:02:09.560
And it's motivating some of them early, particularly
because of the incompetent response to Corona

00:02:09.560 --> 00:02:10.560
virus.

00:02:10.560 --> 00:02:14.510
You've got a lot of fired up Kansas Democrats
who whose enthusiasm for voting in November

00:02:14.510 --> 00:02:16.340
is being reflected in that.

00:02:16.340 --> 00:02:19.140
They are also participating in the Democratic
primary.

00:02:19.140 --> 00:02:20.240
That's possible.

00:02:20.240 --> 00:02:21.340
That's possible.

00:02:21.340 --> 00:02:23.250
But these are massive numbers.

00:02:23.250 --> 00:02:27.840
Again, three and a half times already, the
total turnout from 2016.

00:02:27.840 --> 00:02:32.490
And Trump recently saying on multiple occasions
he doesn't want vote by mail.

00:02:32.490 --> 00:02:35.240
Remember this your back to us here.

00:02:35.240 --> 00:02:41.740
You're saying yesterday about people going
to Wisconsin and voting in the middle of this

00:02:41.740 --> 00:02:43.990
pandemic, really putting their lives on the
line.

00:02:43.990 --> 00:02:50.160
And you said, well, if they do that vote by
mail, perhaps we'll have voter fraud in this

00:02:50.160 --> 00:02:54.930
country as one of our voters in five states,
Utah, Colorado, why Washington and Oregon

00:02:54.930 --> 00:02:59.460
all vote by mail to you or the White House
staff or your campaign provided any evidence

00:02:59.460 --> 00:03:04.070
to back up your claim that mail in voting
is rife with fraud, like the example you gave

00:03:04.070 --> 00:03:06.910
of people working in rooms filling out false
bounce.

00:03:06.910 --> 00:03:12.050
What happened at the beginning of this administration?

00:03:12.050 --> 00:03:13.050
Where's the evidence?

00:03:13.050 --> 00:03:17.470
The I think there's a lot of evidence, but
we'll provide you with some.

00:03:17.470 --> 00:03:18.470
OK.

00:03:18.470 --> 00:03:22.960
And as evidence is being compiled, just like
it's being compiled in the state of California,

00:03:22.960 --> 00:03:28.620
where they settled with Judicial Watch saying
that a million people should not have been

00:03:28.620 --> 00:03:29.620
voting in.

00:03:29.620 --> 00:03:31.640
And you saw that did excuse me wrong.

00:03:31.640 --> 00:03:36.930
I'm just telling you, I'm telling you in California,
in the great state of California, they settled

00:03:36.930 --> 00:03:38.430
and we could have gone a lot further.

00:03:38.430 --> 00:03:44.220
So Trump with no real answers there, because
the reality is vote by mail is not going to

00:03:44.220 --> 00:03:46.000
dramatically increase fraud.

00:03:46.000 --> 00:03:52.200
And then previously, here's Donald Trump admitting
that some of these ideas that Democrats have

00:03:52.200 --> 00:03:57.270
like vote by mail, these would mean Republicans
don't win, which may be true in the sense

00:03:57.270 --> 00:04:02.270
that the more of the will of the people that's
represented at the ballot box, the less likely

00:04:02.270 --> 00:04:06.640
maybe it is that a con man like Donald Trump
would be able to get into the Oval Office.

00:04:06.640 --> 00:04:07.640
Take a look.

00:04:07.640 --> 00:04:08.640
Here's Trump admitting it.

00:04:08.640 --> 00:04:09.640
Just the common fact.

00:04:09.640 --> 00:04:12.810
I mean, they have a majority in the House
and therefore, you need their vote and they

00:04:12.810 --> 00:04:13.880
want to get certain things.

00:04:13.880 --> 00:04:15.099
I will tell you this.

00:04:15.099 --> 00:04:19.159
If you look at before and after the things
they had in there were crazy.

00:04:19.159 --> 00:04:24.830
They had things, levels of voting that if
you ever agree to it, you never have a Republican

00:04:24.830 --> 00:04:27.080
elected in this country again.

00:04:27.080 --> 00:04:34.340
Levels of voting, which if you had would mean
a Republican never gets elected again.

00:04:34.340 --> 00:04:36.309
This is what is being talked about.

00:04:36.309 --> 00:04:39.620
And we are seeing it in Kansas and Republicans.

00:04:39.620 --> 00:04:42.729
No, I mean, look, listen to their credit.

00:04:42.729 --> 00:04:43.969
Republicans aren't wrong.

00:04:43.969 --> 00:04:46.539
They know that if it's easier to vote, it's
not good for them.

00:04:46.539 --> 00:04:50.999
They know that if there is less friction,
if there are fewer obstacles, if the barriers

00:04:50.999 --> 00:04:55.409
to entry to voting are lower, it's not good
for them because the will of the people will

00:04:55.409 --> 00:04:59.499
be more accurately represented by a larger
share.

00:04:59.499 --> 00:05:04.159
Of the population of the United States, we
are seeing an example of it here.

00:05:04.159 --> 00:05:08.599
All the policy that Republicans are pushing
when it comes to how elections are done is

00:05:08.599 --> 00:05:10.909
about suppressing the vote.

00:05:10.909 --> 00:05:16.249
Imagine the damage that vote by mail would
do to Republican efforts to suppress voting.

00:05:16.249 --> 00:05:17.650
Not because of fraud.

00:05:17.650 --> 00:05:19.379
Not because of dead people voting.

00:05:19.379 --> 00:05:20.839
Not because of any of that stuff.

00:05:20.839 --> 00:05:25.770
Simply because a larger share of the population
is casting a ballot.

00:05:25.770 --> 00:05:31.539
So when you look back at the last 15 years,
20 years, I mean, know, redistricting, gerrymandering

00:05:31.539 --> 00:05:33.159
has been going on for a while.

00:05:33.159 --> 00:05:38.330
But when you look at voter I.D. efforts to
reduce early voting, efforts to reduce the

00:05:38.330 --> 00:05:44.219
number of polling places, efforts to purge
voter rolls, voter intimidation at polling

00:05:44.219 --> 00:05:50.949
places, constantly fearmongering about almost
mathematically non-existent double voting

00:05:50.949 --> 00:05:52.530
voter for in-person voter fraud.

00:05:52.530 --> 00:05:55.419
All of that stuff, plus the gerrymandering.

00:05:55.419 --> 00:05:57.159
We now understand why.

00:05:57.159 --> 00:06:03.669
And it's very, very clear all of a sudden
vote by mail would be devastating to Republicans

00:06:03.669 --> 00:06:05.999
and potentially to Donald Trump.

00:06:05.999 --> 00:06:09.129
And so that's why they're going to do everything
they can to stop it.

00:06:09.129 --> 00:06:11.740
Now, let's talk about strategy a little bit.

00:06:11.740 --> 00:06:13.409
This matters more in swing states.

00:06:13.409 --> 00:06:17.610
And what I mean by that is whatever happens
between now and November.

00:06:17.610 --> 00:06:19.860
California is not going to vote for Donald
Trump.

00:06:19.860 --> 00:06:22.880
They're going to vote for Joe Biden, whether
it's vote by mail, whether it's voting in

00:06:22.880 --> 00:06:23.930
person.

00:06:23.930 --> 00:06:26.939
Turnout may be depressed if it's voting in
person and the virus is raging.

00:06:26.939 --> 00:06:29.419
OK, California is not going to be a difference
maker.

00:06:29.419 --> 00:06:31.860
We have an electoral college system.

00:06:31.860 --> 00:06:35.960
If Massachusetts votes by mail or not.

00:06:35.960 --> 00:06:38.839
Trump's not going to win here in Massachusetts.

00:06:38.839 --> 00:06:42.759
The important states are the ones that are
always important in the system that we have.

00:06:42.759 --> 00:06:48.710
We're talking about Michigan, Wisconsin, Pennsylvania,
North Carolina, Florida, the places that could

00:06:48.710 --> 00:06:52.500
turn the election from Trump to Biden or vise
versa.

00:06:52.500 --> 00:06:56.020
That's where we need to be working extra hard
to get vote by mail.

00:06:56.020 --> 00:06:57.289
Who is it going to be up to?

00:06:57.289 --> 00:07:00.969
Well, it's ultimately going to be up to each
individual state.

00:07:00.969 --> 00:07:02.129
It's going to be up to the governor.

00:07:02.129 --> 00:07:06.240
It's going to be up to the state legislatures
in those states.

00:07:06.240 --> 00:07:08.999
This is why, once again, local elections matter.

00:07:08.999 --> 00:07:15.139
When you look at many of the progressive successes
of the 20th century, what made sure that those

00:07:15.139 --> 00:07:19.860
reforms stuck was having a Supreme Court that
would uphold them.

00:07:19.860 --> 00:07:23.369
That's called doing the groundwork and much
the same way.

00:07:23.369 --> 00:07:24.369
What could be the factor?

00:07:24.369 --> 00:07:29.990
I mean, I don't believe it's hyperbolic to
say that the November of twenty twenty election

00:07:29.990 --> 00:07:31.800
could hinge on.

00:07:31.800 --> 00:07:34.749
Is there a Republican or Democratic governor?

00:07:34.749 --> 00:07:40.009
Is there a Republican or Democratic state
legislature, if it ultimately hinges on do

00:07:40.009 --> 00:07:42.659
they get to vote by mail or not?

00:07:42.659 --> 00:07:48.169
Those are decisions that we can go back to
when the state legislatures were elected to

00:07:48.169 --> 00:07:50.659
win the gubernatorial elections happen.

00:07:50.659 --> 00:07:54.929
This is why every election matters and has
to be taken seriously.

00:07:54.929 --> 00:07:55.929
Republicans are scared.

00:07:55.929 --> 00:08:34.330
The numbers in Kansas tell us exactly why
they should

00:08:34.330 --> 00:09:14.380
be scared.

